course: dictionary
lesson: 7835
title: Raccoon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A raccoon is a grey, furry animal from North America. You can spot it by the black mask across its eyes and its bushy, striped tail. Use the clues in the word's context to build your picture of it.
explain: Raccoons are omnivores, so they eat both plants and animals. They are nocturnal, which means they are active at night. Often they wash or feel their food with their front paws. «Foxes trot down city streets at night, raccoons open bins» tells you they are busy after dark.
explain: Never touch or feed a wild raccoon. «Raccoons can bite and carry rabies, so you keep away from them and keep bins closed.» Stay safe by keeping your distance and your bins shut.
fact: A raccoon is a grey, furry animal from North America.
fact: A raccoon has a black "mask" across its eyes and a bushy, striped tail.
fact: Raccoons are omnivores and nocturnal, which means they eat both plants and animals and are active at night.
fact: In the USA and Canada, raccoons often raid rubbish bins, so people keep their bins closed.
fact: Do not touch or feed wild raccoons. They can bite and carry disease.
exercise: «Raccoons can bite and carry rabies, so you keep away from them and keep bins closed.» What should you do? | Feed them with apples | *Keep away from raccoons and keep bins closed | Leave food out for them at night | Pick them up to take them home
exercise: «The animals that win in cities are the clever, bold, eat-almost-anything kind.» What does bold mean here? | Tired and slow | *Brave and fearless | Coloured bright red | Very quiet
exercise: A raccoon has a black marking across its eyes. What is this marking called? | A scar | *A mask | A helmet | A pair of glasses
test: «Raccoons were brought to Europe and some escaped; now they live wild in Germany.» What does wild mean here? | Very fast | *Living free in nature, not kept by people | Very angry | Made of wood
test: Raccoons are active at night. Which word means active at night? | Omnivore | *Nocturnal | Grey | Furry
exam: Why should you not feed a wild raccoon? | They only eat apples and will get sick | *They can bite and carry disease | They will become too small to see | They like being fed by people, so they will follow you home
